    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρατεκταίνομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, prop. of timber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>work into another form</i> : then, generally,
				<i>transform, alter</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ κεν
				ἄλλως Ζεὺς παρατεκτήναιτο</span> not even he could
				<i>make them any way else</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.54
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶψά κε . . ἔπος παρατεκτήναιο</span>
			<i>could disguise, falsify</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.131
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. later in 
				Act.
			, <i>build besides</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			.</div>
